# playpick gave mode=battleground map=conquest spec=druid:guardian style=mash
# view=1280x800 save=fresh. direction.md's #7 has seen mash stall on this exact
# map before (2026-09-27-2.play, druid:balance/carried/touch): mash has no
# steer term in scripts/playbot.ts at all, so it never leaves the pull spot,
# never gets in range of anything, and the match already read hits=0 taken=0
# the whole way for a dps. This is the first tank spec mash has ever been given
# on a battleground -- README says a battleground's five roles are an exact
# trade (one tank, one healer, three damage), so picking the tank spot does not
# add a sixth body, it swaps who is standing in it. If a mashing dps parked at
# the pull spot still let the team's real tank hold the front line, this cell
# removes that tank instead -- worth seeing whether the loss is worse, not just
# repeated, with no actual tank anywhere on the team.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:druid:guardian
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play mash 100
shot mid1
state
bill

wait 5
play mash 100
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play mash 100
shot mid3
state
bill
